	(text "CM5 power-health LED (PI_LED_nPWR, buffered per CM5 datasheet)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.15 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2721df53-c4d4-408d-91d3-228fce1c847b")
	)
	(text "J1/J18: Hirose DF40C-100DS-0.4V(51) module receptacles (LCSC C597931), carried over from the CM4 board.\nBOM / CPL only: their pads are in the A1 footprint. J1 = pads 1-100,\nJ2 = pads 101-200, pin 1 lower left. A1 (CM5): DNP, bought\nseparately, fitted by hand; A1 is also excluded from the position file.\nTO CHECK before ordering: the CM5 datasheet names Amphenol 10164227-1001A1RLF\n(1.5 mm stack) as the mating part, tested to the higher CM5 supply current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 121.92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5a866b58-b35f-4373-ad39-fbf5ed7d5619")
	)
	(text "USB"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 320.04 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "650d97ce-9886-4536-a2ee-a0def6c9f685")
	)
	(text "Module pins 89 (WL_nDisable) \nand 91 (BT_nDisable) are left \nunconnected on purpose (CM5 \ndatasheet Table 4: can be left \nfloating). This board is meant \nfor a CM5 WITHOUT wireless. \nIf a wireless CM5 is ever fitted, \ndisable the radios in config.txt: \ndtoverlay=disable-wifi and\ndtoverlay=disable-bt."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 119.634 109.982 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a55aa2a5-7a23-425b-a0a7-fd6662cd4878")
	)
	(text "CM5"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 23.876 18.288 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 5.08 5.08)
			)
		)
		(uuid "a5c8f753-7318-4504-8c3d-f776f7ce7b69")
	)
	(text "Suggest a CM5004032 (no wireless).\n4GB RAM, 32GB eMMC program storage."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 136.906 17.526 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
		)
		(uuid "ba985d36-30d9-4837-ac45-82bcfec8cd4d")
	)
	(text "From the CM5 Manual:\nActive-low output to \ndrive Power On LED. \nThis signal needs to \nbe buffered."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 118.618 176.276 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "bdcc9427-66dc-4a5c-84a2-0b12157d2c47")
	)
	(text "1PPS from GPS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 137.414 56.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "dae83a57-72fc-4407-8928-42bc039188fd")
	)
	(text "CM5 changes from the CM4 board (CM5 datasheet Table 14):\n- Pins 128-142 and 157-171 (CSI0 / DSI0 on the CM4) are the two USB 3.0 ports. TX pairs are AC-coupled on the module.\n- Pin 111 VBUS_EN (active high) enables the USB 3.0 port power switch.\n- Pins 94/96 are CC1/CC2 (USB-C PD supply negotiation), not ADC inputs: the AIN0/AIN1 inputs are gone.\n- Pin 100 is CAM_GPIO1 (no nEXTRST), pin 92 is PWR_Button, pin 99 is PMIC_Enable (was GLOBAL_EN), pin 76 is VBAT (RTC).\n- Pin 101 USB_OTG_ID is left open (pulled up on the module): the USB 2.0 port on USB-C is a device port for rpiboot only.\nGPIO use: GPIO12/13 = UART to the STM32 (UART4 on the CM5), GPIO23 = MCU_RST (high = hold STM32 in reset),\nGPIO24 = MCU_BOOT0 (high = STM32 system bootloader), GPIO25 = USB_nFAULT (low = USB port over-current)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300.99 140 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.016 1.016)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ea9a1faa-1c4b-4382-8f62-c13da9347827")
	)
